@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# GK1 EXEC0198 — Source-verified Classic TAX Spring-kernel what-if
+
+Preserved all inherited EXEC0197 C11 gameplay, 14/27 country original evidence, controller TAX/ASSIGN/PASS, private GC19 saves/cold-load, and Enhanced-only abilities. Same native graphical executable now displays a **live, rate-sensitive numeric tax forecast** in the Classic TAX controller screen. Uses actual replay-validated Classic worker allocations and exact original source-authenticated checkpoint, and the pre-existing independently traced Spring FOOD/TAX/PAYROLL kernel (`gk75_spring_food_tax_pay`), with no hardcoded country values or merchant offers. Rates 1..100; app never writes original country bytes from this preview. Synthetic invalid sources, corrupted replay, invalid rate and arithmetic overflow fail closed and leave the output unchanged.
+
+**Important scope:** an isolated one-pass computation with hypothetical constant source-derived country fields, **NOT next season**, original ruler attribute costs, population/age/RNG/events/AI, and **NOT an independently generated original first Spring**. Display current/proposed gross tax and post-kernel net gold as *what-if* only. Original Classic command tax selection is still experimental/manual-derived.
+
+Build: `cmake -S execution_198 -B build198 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build build198 -j8 && ctest --test-dir build198 --output-on-failure -j8` from complete historical archive root. UI smoke: `xvfb-run -a build198/gk1_native_shell --smoke-classic-tax-original /PRIVATE/stock_source 120`. Original raw NES sources are NEVER distributed. Win32/NSIS/physical controller and full campaigns NOT RUN.
